# NOTICE

This project includes software and materials that originated in the AERPAW
project's E-VM software profile and aerpawlib vehicle control library.

## AERPAW E-VM materials

The following directories contain material derived from the AERPAW E-VM
(`AHN/E-VM`) and C-VM (`AHN/C-VM`) software trees:

- `vendor/aerpaw-profile/AHN/E-VM/Profile_software/`
- `vendor/aerpaw-profile/AHN/E-VM/bin/`
- `vendor/aerpaw-profile/AHN/C-VM/MAVLink_Filter/Geofences/`

These were copied from the AERPAW project development repository and are
retained here so that AERPAW-style `aerpawlib` experiment scripts and the
AERPAW profile filesystem layout (start/stop scripts, `bin` helpers, and
geofence definitions) remain compatible with this digital twin deployment.

Binary and generated artifacts from the original tree (APK builds, telemetry
logs, radio captures, result data, images, and bytecode caches) have been
removed. Only source code, configuration, and data files that are exercised by
the emulator remain.

The AERPAW project is developed by the AERPAW team at North Carolina State
University: https://aerpaw.org/

## aerpawlib

`vendor/aerpawlib/` contains a copy of the `aerpawlib` package as used in the
AERPAW E-VM profile at the time this project was developed. The current
public `aerpawlib` release (github.com/AERPAW/aerpawlib) differs substantially
from this copy; this project intentionally vendors the version that matches
the E-VM profile layout.

## Other third-party components

The Docker images build from public upstream sources:

- ArduPilot SITL (forked at github.com/morzack/ardupilot, used for the
  `aerpaw-4.3.6` vehicle branch)
- MAVLink Router (github.com/mavlink-router/mavlink-router)
- dronekit-python (forked at github.com/morzack/dronekit-python)

